        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francine McDougall, Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, Melissa George\n- Products: Sugar & Spice, Go Figure, Cow Belles\n- Roles: film director, film producer, photographer, television director, television producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: teen crime comedy films, Disney Channel Original Movies\n\nFacts:\n- Francine McDougall is an Australian film director, film producer, photographer, television director, television producer, and screenwriter.\n- In 2001, Francine McDougall made her feature film directorial debut by directing the comedy film Sugar & Spice.\n- Sugar & Spice is a 2001 American teen crime comedy film directed by Francine McDougall and starring Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, and Melissa George.\n- The plot of Sugar & Spice follows a group of high school cheerleaders who commit armed robbery after one of them becomes pregnant and needs money.\n- Francine McDougall is best known for directing Sugar & Spice.\n- In 2005, Francine McDougall directed the Disney Channel Original Movie Go Figure.\n- In 2006, Francine McDougall directed the Disney Channel Original Movie Cow Belles.",
